@startuml
' drevops/behat-steps - data flow for generating the step documentation.
' Traced from docs.php functions main, extract_info, parse_class_comment,
' parse_method_comment, extract_method_steps, validate, validate_tags,
' tag_registry, render_info, replace_content.
' Regenerate every SVG with:  plantuml -tsvg docs/architecture/*.puml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title Data flow: STEPS.md generation

participant "ahoy update-docs\nahoy lint-docs" as Dev
participant "docs.php main()" as Main
participant "extract_info()" as Extract
participant "Test FeatureContext" as Ctx
participant "validate()\nvalidate_tags()" as Validate
participant "render_info()\nreplace_content()" as Render

Dev -> Main: php docs.php [~--fail-on-change]
activate Main
Main -> Main: require build/vendor/autoload.php\nand the FeatureContext bootstrap

Main -> Extract: extract_info(FeatureContext::class)
activate Extract
Extract -> Ctx: ReflectionClass::getTraits()
activate Ctx
Ctx --> Extract: every composed trait
deactivate Ctx
Extract -> Extract: scan src/ for trait files\nand match them off
Extract -> Extract: keep public methods prefixed with\nthe trait name that carry a step attribute
Extract -> Extract: parse the docblock for the\ndescription and the @code example
Extract -> Extract: derive Generic or Drupal\nfrom the file's directory

alt a trait file was never composed in
  Extract -> Main: throw Exception(not found in the class)
end
Extract --> Main: step info
deactivate Extract

Main -> Validate: validate(info), validate_tags(info)
activate Validate
note right of Validate
  When needs "I ", Then needs "should"
  and an Assert method name, one step
  attribute per method, an example is
  mandatory, tags must match tag_registry()
end note
alt errors found
  Validate --> Main: error list
  Main --> Dev: print errors, exit 1
else clean
  Validate --> Main: no errors
end
deactivate Validate

Main -> Render: render_info(info)
activate Render
Render -> Render: swap the block between the heading\nand the [//]: # (END) marker
Render --> Main: STEPS.md and README.md contents
deactivate Render

alt contents are unchanged
  Main --> Dev: exit 0, documentation is up to date
else contents differ, with ~--fail-on-change
  Main --> Dev: exit 1, documentation is outdated, nothing written
else contents differ, update mode
  Main --> Dev: write STEPS.md and README.md
end
deactivate Main
@enduml
